2D Array 

Find the Row with Maximum 1s in a Sorted Binary Matrix

# brute force method, linear search for every element in the array 
# optimal way, binary search 

The correct code starts at the top-right corner and moves left whenever it hits a 1, immediately updating the winning row index (answer = row). If it hits a 0,
it moves down to search the next row while keeping that left-side boundary. 
This guarantees that the last row to successfully push the boundary left is correctly captured before the loop ends.
